===Alternative forms===
* {{l|fr|debte}} {{q|obsolete}}
* {{l|fr|dête}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{der|fr|fro|dete}}, from {{der|fr|la|dēbita}}, plural of {{m|la|dēbitum}}. {{doublet|fr|débit}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|Fr-dette.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f}}

# [[debt]]

====Usage notes====
While both {{m|fr|dette}} and {{m|fr|créance}} correspond with English {{m|en|debt}}, {{m|fr|dette}} is seen from the perspective of the borrower (money they owe), whereas {{m|fr|créance}} is seen from the perspective of the lender (money owed to them).

